## Tool Selection

### Always Use Invar For:
```bash
invar sig <file>           # See contracts (UNIQUE: shows @pre/@post)
invar map --top 20         # Find entry points (UNIQUE: reference count ranking)
invar guard --changed      # Verify code quality (REQUIRED)
```

### Task-Based Selection:

| I want to... | Tool | Fallback if unavailable |
|--------------|------|-------------------------|
| See contracts/patterns | `invar sig <file>` | — (only Invar shows contracts) |
| Find hot spots/entry points | `invar map --top 20` | — (only Invar has ref counts) |
| Find specific symbol | Serena `find_symbol` | `invar map` + grep |
| Find who calls this | Serena `find_referencing_symbols` | `invar map` (shows ref count) |
| Edit function body | Serena `replace_symbol_body` | Standard file edit |
| Rename across project | Serena `rename_symbol` | Manual search & replace |
| Verify after changes | `invar guard --changed` | — (always use Invar) |

**Rule:** `invar sig` before reading code. Contracts tell you more than implementation.

